From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:51:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 86/99] v8: e2k: take rbranch into deferred code only when it
 calls

Deferred is a layout hint, not a frequency. A taken rbranch costs 14
cycles against 6 of an ordinary branch, so a branch into deferred code is
made rare only when the deferred code reachable from the target (up to
16 blocks) calls, deoptimizes or aborts; deferred code that only computes
and goes back to ordinary code (the Smi case of ToBooleanForBaselineJump)
gets an ordinary branch.
---
 .../backend/e2k/code-generator-e2k.cc         | 47 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chromium/v8/src/compiler/backend/e2k/code-generator-e2k.cc b/chromium/v8/src/compiler/backend/e2k/code-generator-e2k.cc
index 9596a3a0c5..efbe131b33 100644
--- a/chromium/v8/src/compiler/backend/e2k/code-generator-e2k.cc
+++ b/chromium/v8/src/compiler/backend/e2k/code-generator-e2k.cc
@@ -4721,6 +4721,50 @@ void AssembleBranchToLabels(CodeGenerator* gen, MacroAssembler* masm,
 #define __ masm()->
